{"vid":"PGveO2PGzEw","source":"PGveO2PGzEw.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.2,"txt":"Yellowhead shits. I don't want to know."},{"t":2.7,"txt":"This is what matters. I can't rule the"},{"t":5.7,"txt":"kingdoms if the Starks and the"},{"t":7.4,"txt":"Lannisters are at each other's throats."},{"t":9.4,"txt":"So, enough."},{"t":12.2,"txt":">> Stop describing conflict like a textbook"},{"t":14.9,"txt":"robot. Master the cutthroat, aggressive"},{"t":18.2,"txt":"vocabulary of Westeros to dominate your"},{"t":21,"txt":"next heated debate."},{"t":24.2,"txt":"[music]"},{"t":28.8,"txt":"When I was 12, I milked my eel into a"},{"t":31.9,"txt":"pot of turtle stew. I flog the oneeyed"},{"t":35.5,"txt":"snake. I skinned my sausage. I made the"},{"t":39.2,"txt":"bald man cry"},{"t":41.7,"txt":"into the turtle stew."},{"t":46.5,"txt":"This when I was 12, I milked my eel into"},{"t":50.2,"txt":"a pot of turtle stew."},{"t":52.4,"txt":">> Milked my eel."},{"t":54.4,"txt":"Milked my eel is a highly creative,"},{"t":56.5,"txt":"crude euphemism for masturbation. In"},{"t":59.2,"txt":"advanced English, speakers often invent"},{"t":61.4,"txt":"colorful metaphorical phrases to discuss"},{"t":63.5,"txt":"taboo subjects without using clinical or"},{"t":66.1,"txt":"explicit terms. It demonstrates"},{"t":68.4,"txt":"linguistic creativity rather than"},{"t":70.6,"txt":"standard vocabulary."},{"t":73,"txt":"He spent the whole afternoon polishing"},{"t":74.7,"txt":"the bishop instead of working. It uses a"},{"t":77.7,"txt":"similar creative structure to imply"},{"t":79.4,"txt":"wasting time on a private act."},{"t":83,"txt":"part of turtle steel. My flogged the"},{"t":86.2,"txt":"oneeyed snake is skinned."},{"t":88.2,"txt":">> Flogged the oneeyed snake."},{"t":90.8,"txt":"Fogged the oneeyed snake creates a"},{"t":92.6,"txt":"vivid, albeit grotesque, visual"},{"t":95,"txt":"metaphor. The verb fogg means to beat or"},{"t":97.7,"txt":"whip, adding an aggressive connotation"},{"t":99.7,"txt":"to the act. C2 learners should recognize"},{"t":102.6,"txt":"this pattern of combining violent verbs"},{"t":104.6,"txt":"with phallic nouns and slang."},{"t":107.6,"txt":"Stop choking the chicken and come help"},{"t":109.2,"txt":"me with the dishes."},{"t":111,"txt":"It uses a violent verb and animal noun"},{"t":113,"txt":"to humorously refer to the same act."},{"t":117,"txt":">> The oneeyed snake skinned my sausage. I"},{"t":121.1,"txt":">> skinned my sausage."},{"t":123.5,"txt":"Skinned my sausage relies on"},{"t":125.2,"txt":"alliteration, the repetition of the s"},{"t":127.5,"txt":"sound to make the slang catchy and"},{"t":129.5,"txt":"memorable."},{"t":131,"txt":"Native speakers often prefer slang that"},{"t":133.1,"txt":"has a rhythmic or poetic quality, even"},{"t":135.4,"txt":"when discussing crude topics. It adds a"},{"t":138.1,"txt":"comedic effect to the confession."},{"t":141,"txt":"He's just spanking the monkey in his"},{"t":142.6,"txt":"room. It shows how rhyme or rhythm makes"},{"t":145.4,"txt":"slang phrases stick in the mind."},{"t":153.1,"txt":"But is it wise to yank the lion's tail?"},{"t":155.3,"txt":"Tywin Lannister is the richest man in"},{"t":156.8,"txt":"all the seven kingdoms."},{"t":160.2,"txt":">> Gold wins wars, not soldiers."},{"t":166.2,"txt":"Admirable, but is it wise to yank the"},{"t":168.9,"txt":"lion's tail? Diamond L."},{"t":170.4,"txt":">> Yank the lion's tail."},{"t":172.9,"txt":"To yank the lion's tail is a powerful"},{"t":176,"txt":"idiom meaning to deliberately provoke a"},{"t":178.6,"txt":"dangerous or powerful enemy. It suggests"},{"t":181.8,"txt":"an action that is bold but potentially"},{"t":184.3,"txt":"suicidal. Use this when someone is"},{"t":187.1,"txt":"taking an unnecessary risk against a"},{"t":189.8,"txt":"superior force."},{"t":192.4,"txt":"Suing the massive corporation was like"},{"t":194.6,"txt":"yanking the lion's tail. It describes a"},{"t":198.2,"txt":"small entity provoking a much larger"},{"t":201,"txt":"dangerous one."},{"t":203.4,"txt":"Don't yank the lion's tail unless you"},{"t":205.5,"txt":"have a plan to escape the teeth. It"},{"t":208.7,"txt":"warns against provocation without a"},{"t":211.1,"txt":"backup plan."},{"t":215.4,"txt":">> Gold wins wars, not soldiers. And how"},{"t":218.6,"txt":"come Robert"},{"t":219.3,"txt":">> Gold wins wars."},{"t":222,"txt":"Gold wins wars is a matonomy where gold"},{"t":225.3,"txt":"represents economic power and funding."},{"t":228.2,"txt":"It argues that resources are more"},{"t":230.5,"txt":"decisive than manpower. You can use"},{"t":233.1,"txt":"similar structures like money talks or"},{"t":235.7,"txt":"wallets vote in debates about economics"},{"t":238.3,"txt":"and influence."},{"t":240.6,"txt":"In modern elections, ad spend wins"},{"t":243,"txt":"votes, not handshakes."},{"t":245.8,"txt":"It claims that financial resources"},{"t":248,"txt":"overpower traditional methods."},{"t":254.9,"txt":"Yellowhead shits. I don't want to know."},{"t":257.5,"txt":"This is what matters. I can't rule the"},{"t":260.4,"txt":"kingdoms if the Starks and the"},{"t":262.2,"txt":"Lannisters are at each other's throats."},{"t":264.2,"txt":"So, enough"},{"t":269.4,"txt":"far."},{"t":271.1,"txt":"I don't know what happened between you"},{"t":272.7,"txt":"and those yellowhaired shits. I don't"},{"t":275,"txt":"want"},{"t":275.3,"txt":">> yellowhaired shits."},{"t":277.4,"txt":"Yellow-haired shits is a derogatory,"},{"t":279.4,"txt":"dismissive slur based on physical"},{"t":281.1,"txt":"appearance. While rude, it teaches how"},{"t":283.5,"txt":"compound adjectives yellow-haired are"},{"t":285.6,"txt":"combined with profanity to show contempt"},{"t":287.9,"txt":"for a specific group's vanity or"},{"t":289.7,"txt":"heritage. It effectively conveys the"},{"t":292.2,"txt":"speaker's total lack of respect."},{"t":295.1,"txt":"I'm not listening to those silver spoon"},{"t":296.8,"txt":"jerks anymore. It insults a group based"},{"t":299.6,"txt":"on their privilege and behavior."},{"t":303.2,"txt":"s and the Lannisters are at each other's"},{"t":304.8,"txt":"throats. So enough."},{"t":308.2,"txt":">> At each other's throats."},{"t":310.4,"txt":"To be at each other's throats implies"},{"t":312.2,"txt":"violent, vicious conflict, not just a"},{"t":314.6,"txt":"simple disagreement. It creates an image"},{"t":316.9,"txt":"of predatory animals fighting to kill."},{"t":319.4,"txt":"Use this to describe relationships or"},{"t":321.2,"txt":"rivalries that have become aggressively"},{"t":322.9,"txt":"hostile."},{"t":324.6,"txt":"The marketing and sales departments have"},{"t":326.3,"txt":"been at each other's throats all"},{"t":327.6,"txt":"quarter. It describes intense aggressive"},{"t":330.6,"txt":"internal conflict within a company."},{"t":343.7,"txt":"again and all those who shared in his"},{"t":345.8,"txt":"crimes. I denounce him and attain him. I"},{"t":351,"txt":"strip him of all ranks and titles."},{"t":358.6,"txt":"I charge you to bring the king's justice"},{"t":360.7,"txt":"to the false knights Gregor Clegane and"},{"t":362.9,"txt":"all those who shared in"},{"t":364.2,"txt":">> I charge you"},{"t":366.2,"txt":"I charge you is a formal authoritative"},{"t":369.1,"txt":"way to give an official command or duty."},{"t":372.2,"txt":"It is much heavier than ask or tell. It"},{"t":375.8,"txt":"implies a legal or moral obligation is"},{"t":378.6,"txt":"being placed upon the listener."},{"t":380.8,"txt":"Excellent for C2 formal contexts."},{"t":385,"txt":"I charged this committee with finding a"},{"t":387.1,"txt":"solution by Friday."},{"t":389.4,"txt":"It formally assigns a serious"},{"t":391.4,"txt":"responsibility to a group."},{"t":395.2,"txt":">> His crimes, I denounce him and attain"},{"t":399.2,"txt":"him."},{"t":400.2,"txt":">> Attain."},{"t":402.2,"txt":"Attain is a rare archaic legal verb"},{"t":405.4,"txt":"meaning to declare someone a traitor and"},{"t":407.8,"txt":"strip them of all civil rights and"},{"t":409.7,"txt":"property. While you won't use it at a"},{"t":412,"txt":"coffee shop, recognizing such specific"},{"t":414.8,"txt":"legal terminology is a hallmark of C2"},{"t":417.8,"txt":"proficiency in historical or legal"},{"t":420.3,"txt":"texts."},{"t":422.4,"txt":"The relentless media coverage"},{"t":424.3,"txt":"practically attained him before the"},{"t":426.3,"txt":"trial even began. It metaphorically"},{"t":429.8,"txt":"suggests he was stripped of his"},{"t":431.4,"txt":"reputation without due process."},{"t":435.9,"txt":"him. I strip him of all ranks and"},{"t":439.7,"txt":"titles."},{"t":441,"txt":">> Strip him of."},{"t":443.1,"txt":"To strip someone of something is a"},{"t":445.4,"txt":"strong collocation used when removing"},{"t":447.7,"txt":"honors, power, or dignity. It implies a"},{"t":451.6,"txt":"forceful, humiliating, and total"},{"t":454,"txt":"removal. It is commonly used in"},{"t":456.6,"txt":"political, military, or corporate"},{"t":458.7,"txt":"scandals."},{"t":460.7,"txt":"After the scandal, the board decided to"},{"t":463.2,"txt":"strip the CEO of his bonuses."},{"t":466.2,"txt":"It describes the forceful removal of"},{"t":468.6,"txt":"financial rewards due to misconduct."},{"t":477.3,"txt":"Sometimes possession"},{"t":480.2,"txt":"is an abstract concept."},{"t":483.9,"txt":"When they captured me, they took my"},{"t":485.7,"txt":"purse, but the GOLD IS STILL MINE."},{"t":488.6,"txt":"RIGHT."},{"t":493.4,"txt":"WHEN THEY CAPTURED ME, they took my"},{"t":495.2,"txt":"purse. But the gold is still mine."},{"t":498.9,"txt":"Purse."},{"t":500.6,"txt":"Purse here doesn't just mean a handbag."},{"t":503.6,"txt":"Historically and metaphorically, it"},{"t":505.4,"txt":"refers to one's total financial"},{"t":507,"txt":"resources or wealth. In boxing or"},{"t":509.5,"txt":"competitions, the purse is the prize"},{"t":511.4,"txt":"money. It allows you to speak about"},{"t":513.4,"txt":"wealth in a more abstract way."},{"t":516.3,"txt":"The fighters are competing for a purse"},{"t":517.9,"txt":"of $2 million."},{"t":520,"txt":"It refers to the total prize money"},{"t":521.6,"txt":"available in a competition."},{"t":525,"txt":"The gold is still mine."},{"t":527.4,"txt":"The gold is still mine plays on the"},{"t":529,"txt":"concept that ownership is a mental"},{"t":530.6,"txt":"construct, not just physical holding."},{"t":533.1,"txt":"This sentence challenges the idea of"},{"t":534.8,"txt":"theft. Use this rhetorical style when"},{"t":537.8,"txt":"you want to assert rights over something"},{"t":539.3,"txt":"you have lost physical control of."},{"t":542.3,"txt":"They stole my laptop, but the ideas"},{"t":544,"txt":"inside it are still mine. It asserts"},{"t":546.7,"txt":"intellectual ownership despite physical"},{"t":548.6,"txt":"loss."},{"t":556.1,"txt":">> Tell him I want what was bargained for."},{"t":557.7,"txt":"I'm taking you back. [music]"},{"t":560.2,"txt":">> She can keep the baby."},{"t":562.4,"txt":">> I'll cut it out and leave it for him."},{"t":570.5,"txt":"Tell him I want what was bargained for."},{"t":572.2,"txt":"I'm taking you back. [music]"},{"t":574.6,"txt":"He can keep the bargained for."},{"t":577.5,"txt":"To get what was bargained for refers to"},{"t":580.5,"txt":"the specific terms of an agreement, but"},{"t":583.3,"txt":"often implies getting more trouble than"},{"t":585.6,"txt":"expected, eg more than I bargained for."},{"t":589.6,"txt":"Here, it's literal. It's a great phrase"},{"t":592.1,"txt":"to use when demanding someone honor the"},{"t":594.3,"txt":"exact details of a deal."},{"t":597.5,"txt":"This stressful commute is more than I"},{"t":599.6,"txt":"bargained for when I took the job. It"},{"t":602.7,"txt":"expresses that the negative aspects were"},{"t":605.3,"txt":"not expected or agreed to."},{"t":610.9,"txt":">> I'll cut it out and leave it for him."},{"t":613.1,"txt":"[music]"},{"t":614.3,"txt":">> Cut it out."},{"t":616.3,"txt":"Cut it out usually means stop it. Eg."},{"t":620,"txt":"Stop being annoying. However, here it is"},{"t":623,"txt":"used literally and brutally to mean"},{"t":625.5,"txt":"removing something surgically. This poly"},{"t":628.6,"txt":"semi creates a chilling effect. It"},{"t":631.4,"txt":"reminds C2 learners to never assume a"},{"t":633.9,"txt":"phrase is idiomatic without checking the"},{"t":636.6,"txt":"context."},{"t":638.6,"txt":"If you don't cut it out with the noise,"},{"t":640.6,"txt":"I'm leaving. It uses the common"},{"t":643.8,"txt":"idiomatic meaning of stop doing that."},{"t":647.6,"txt":"The surgeon had to cut the infection out"},{"t":650,"txt":"immediately."},{"t":651.7,"txt":"It uses the literal physical meaning of"},{"t":654.2,"txt":"removal."},{"t":656.9,"txt":">> Great job watching till the end. If you"},{"t":659.1,"txt":"enjoyed it, show some love with a like."},{"t":661.6,"txt":"[music] See you next time."}],"words":[{"t":0.16,"w":"Yellowhead"},{"t":0.88,"w":"shits."},{"t":1.439,"w":"I"},{"t":1.68,"w":"don't"},{"t":1.839,"w":"want"},{"t":2,"w":"to"},{"t":2.24,"w":"know."},{"t":2.72,"w":"This"},{"t":2.96,"w":"is"},{"t":3.04,"w":"what"},{"t":3.36,"w":"matters."},{"t":4.4,"w":"I"},{"t":4.72,"w":"can't"},{"t":4.96,"w":"rule"},{"t":5.359,"w":"the"},{"t":5.68,"w":"kingdoms"},{"t":6.319,"w":"if"},{"t":6.56,"w":"the"},{"t":6.799,"w":"Starks"},{"t":7.2,"w":"and"},{"t":7.279,"w":"the"},{"t":7.44,"w":"Lannisters"},{"t":7.919,"w":"are"},{"t":8.08,"w":"at"},{"t":8.24,"w":"each"},{"t":8.4,"w":"other's"},{"t":8.72,"w":"throats."},{"t":9.44,"w":"So,"},{"t":9.92,"w":"enough."},{"t":12.24,"w":">>"},{"t":12.24,"w":"Stop"},{"t":12.639,"w":"describing"},{"t":13.36,"w":"conflict"},{"t":13.84,"w":"like"},{"t":14.08,"w":"a"},{"t":14.32,"w":"textbook"},{"t":14.88,"w":"robot."},{"t":16.16,"w":"Master"},{"t":16.56,"w":"the"},{"t":16.8,"w":"cutthroat,"},{"t":17.6,"w":"aggressive"},{"t":18.16,"w":"vocabulary"},{"t":18.8,"w":"of"},{"t":19.039,"w":"Westeros"},{"t":19.92,"w":"to"},{"t":20.16,"w":"dominate"},{"t":20.64,"w":"your"},{"t":20.96,"w